# Local dev secrets for agent-atlas.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (already gitignored) and fill in real values
# for `wrangler dev`. For deploy, the equivalent goes in via
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>`, never in wrangler.jsonc `vars`.
#
# AI Gateway auth: when an AI Gateway is called through the Workers AI binding
# (`env.AI.run(..., { gateway })`, which is how every model call in this repo
# is made), the request is pre-authenticated by the account the Worker runs
# under. The `cf-aig-authorization` token / "Authenticated Gateway" setting
# only applies to calls made directly against the Gateway's REST/Universal
# endpoint (a plain `fetch` to the gateway URL), which this codebase does not
# do.
#
# Net effect: no secret is required here for the "atlas" AI Gateway to work
# locally or in production, as long as every call continues to go through the
# AI binding. If a future ticket adds a direct REST call to the Gateway
# (bypassing the binding), add the token here as e.g.:
#   AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
#
# This file intentionally has no keys today — it exists so the "nothing
# needed" conclusion is discoverable instead of re-investigated per ticket.
# Copied from agent-helios, whose version reached the same conclusion first.
